# Whitelist approach: ignore everything at the repo root by default, then
# explicitly allow only the folders/files that belong in the shared repo.
# This keeps internal docs out WITHOUT naming them here (so the .gitignore
# itself reveals nothing about local-only files).

/*

# Things that SHOULD be tracked:
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/phase0-spike/
!/wdk-wallet-concordium/

# Within the tracked folders, still ignore dependencies and local run artifacts:
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
callback.txt
onboard-state.json
identity-object.json
identity-request.json
